  <section class='content-section'>
    <div class='topic-section'>
      <h2>Optimizing Control Flow Performance with AI</h2>
      <p class='mb-2'>Just like accessibility, AI doesn't automatically optimize for performance. When I asked AI to "clean up" my loops, it sometimes made them slower by using elegant but inefficient patterns. Prof. Teeters taught me to be explicit about performance requirements.</p>

      <h3 class='mt-3'>The Performance-Focused Prompt</h3>
      <div class='prompt-box mt-2'>
        <div class='prompt-label'>✅ Performance Optimization Prompt:</div>
        <CodeBlock
          code={`Optimize this loop for performance with these requirements:

Performance constraints:
- Must handle arrays with 1000+ items without visible lag
- Minimize DOM updates (batch changes when possible)
- Use early return/break when match is found
- Avoid creating new functions inside the loop

Current code:
[paste your loop code]

Goal: Find the first skill that matches a search term, then stop.
Currently it checks every item even after finding a match.`}
          lang='text'
        />
      </div>

      <h3 class='mt-3'>Before and After: Performance Comparison</h3>

      <div class='warning-box mt-2'>
        <h3>❌ Loop That Checks Everything (Slow)</h3>
        <CodeBlock
          code={`// Checks ALL items even after finding match
function findSkill(skills, searchTerm) {
    let result = null;
    for (let i = 0; i < skills.length; i++) {
        if (skills[i].toLowerCase().includes(searchTerm.toLowerCase())) {
            result = skills[i];
            // Keeps looping! Wastes time on remaining items
        }
    }
    return result;
}
/* ❌ Checks all 1000 items even if match is first */
/* ❌ Creates toLowerCase() on every iteration */`}
          lang='javascript'
        />
      </div>

      <div class='prompt-box mt-2'>
        <div class='prompt-label'>✅ Optimized Loop with Early Return</div>
        <CodeBlock
          code={`// Stops immediately when match is found
function findSkill(skills, searchTerm) {
    const search = searchTerm.toLowerCase(); // Calculate once!

    for (let i = 0; i < skills.length; i++) {
        if (skills[i].toLowerCase().includes(search)) {
            return skills[i]; // Found it! Stop immediately.
        }
    }
    return null; // Only reached if no match found
}
/* ✅ Early return stops loop on first match */
/* ✅ Search term lowercased once, not 1000 times */`}
          lang='javascript'
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

